    <innerclass refid="structUploader_1_1Io" prot="public">Uploader::Io</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceUploader">Uploader</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>The Gateway&apos;s firmware uploader (#366) — stages an image the client streams over USB, then flashes a board&apos;s bootloader over CAN through <ref refid="namespacePanelBridge" kindref="compound">PanelBridge</ref>, on its own. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Library-internal: <ref refid="SimGateway_8cpp" kindref="compound">SimGateway.cpp</ref> feeds it the client&apos;s UPL_* frames, every line <ref refid="namespacePanelBridge" kindref="compound">PanelBridge</ref> sends the host, and a tick from loop(); the uploader answers through the callbacks in <ref refid="structUploader_1_1Io" kindref="compound">Uploader::Io</ref>. Portable C++ — no Arduino, no globals of the caller&apos;s — so it can be exercised off-target.</para>
<para>Contract: FirmwarePlan/07-simgateway-api.md § <ref refid="namespaceUploader" kindref="compound">Uploader</ref>, <ref refid="UploadProtocol_8h" kindref="compound">UploadProtocol.h</ref>, <ref refid="BootProtocol_8h" kindref="compound">BootProtocol.h</ref>.</para>
